{"abstract":"IT developers and consultants often ask for an exemplary requirements specification as a starting point for their own project. Problem-oriented requirements SL-07 is such a specification. It is a template filled in with a complex example: Requirements for an Electronic Health Record system (EHR). There is a matching contract. This booklet explains why the requirements are written the way they are, what to be careful about, how the requirements relate to business, the contract, etc. You can download the requirements template, the contract, and an on-line version of this guide here: http://www.itu.dk/people/slauesen/SorenReqs.html#SL-07","author_count":1,"contributors":["Lauesen, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381467"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Contract management","Electronic Health Record EHR","Requirements specification","Template","business alignment"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"problem oriented requirements sl 000000000007 guide and contract version 000000000009","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.amazon.com/Problem-oriented-Requirements-SL-07-Contract-Version/dp/B09TMZ3LMF","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381467","ids":["itu-0d5a17d2-2321-4d72-b996-2eccf4ac0499"],"keyword":["Electronic Health Record (EHR)","business alignment","contract management","requirements specification","template"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A76575547872DF7CA41C73693E1E355F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"lauesenpau","last":"Lauesen","locid":"ea6d10cf-6bb5-4414-8966-f1ed2591f794","name":"Lauesen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-2300-6934","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9798425802224"],"pages":"128","publisher":"Amazon Kindle","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0d5a17d2-2321-4d72-b996-2eccf4ac0499"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Problem-oriented Requirements SL-07 Guide and Contract Version 9","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381467","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"User stories are widely used in Agile development as requirements. However, few studies have assessed the quality of user stories in practice. (2) Methods: What is the quality of user stories in practice? To answer the research question, we conducted a case study. We used an analysis report from a real-life project where an organization wanted to improve its existing hotline system or acquire a new one. We invited IT practitioners to write requirements for the new system based on the analysis report, user stories, and whatever else they considered necessary. The practitioners could ask the authors questions as they would ask a customer in a real setting. We evaluated the practitioners’ replies using these IEEE 830 quality criteria: completeness, correctness, verifiability, and traceability. (3) Results: The replies covered only 33% of the needs and wishes in the analysis report. Further, the replies largely missed other requirements needed in most projects, such as learnability and maintainability. Incorrect or restrictive solutions were often proposed by the practitioners. Most replies included user stories that were hard to verify, or would have caused a cumbersome user interface if implemented independently. (4) Conclusion: In this project, relying on the user stories would have been a disaster. Although the user stories could have been improved, they wouldn’t cover the necessary requirements in the project.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Lauesen, Søren","Kuhail, Mohammad Amin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383356"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Case study","User stories","hotline support","problem oriented requirements"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"user story quality in practice a case study","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/software1030010","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383356","ids":["itu-8e1a42af-b862-45b4-be74-966469245f8d"],"keyword":["User stories","case study","hotline support","problem-oriented requirements"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-5B3307DE3C75DABE22729F2C630443C8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/software1030010","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"lauesenpau","last":"Lauesen","locid":"ea6d10cf-6bb5-4414-8966-f1ed2591f794","name":"Lauesen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-2300-6934","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammad Amin","key":"kuhailpau","last":"Kuhail","name":"Kuhail, Mohammad Amin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/software1030010","issn":["2674113X"],"issue":"3","journal":"Software","pages":"223-243","publisher":"MDPI","status":"p","title":"Software","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8e1a42af-b862-45b4-be74-966469245f8d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"User Story Quality in Practice: A Case Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383356","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Existing approaches to data visualization are one of these two: accessible to end-user developers but limited in customizability, or inaccessible and expressive. For instance, commercial charting tools are easy to use, but support only predened visualizations, while programmatic visualization tools support custom visualizations, but require advanced programming skills. We show that it is possible to combine the learnability of charting tools and the expressiveness of visualization tools. Uvis is an interactive visualization and user interface design tool that targets end-user developers with skills comparable to spreadsheet formulas. With Uvis, designers drag and drop visual objects, set visual properties to formulas, and see the result immediately. The formulas are declarative and similar to spreadsheet formulas. The formulas compute the property values and can refer to data from database, visual objects, and end-user input. To substantiate our claim, we compared Uvis with popular visualization tools. Further, we conducted usability studies that test the ability of designers to customize visualizations with our approach. Our results show that end-user developers can learn the basics of Uvis relatively fast.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Kuhail, Mohammad Amin","Lauesen, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382454"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"country":["United Arab Emirates"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Zayed University"],"keyword":["End User Development","Information visualization","Visualization Tools","formulas"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"uvis a formula based end user tool for data visualization","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2020.3002591","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382454","identifier":[{"id":"85087402232","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-4f38ee1b-a4e6-4929-86fb-8baaa54b7d34"],"keyword":["End-user development","formulas","information visualization","visualization tools"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-290624F489A05FC7A76DDF94F2800F9E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2020.3002591","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85351704/Uvis.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ae","key":"zayed university","loc":["United Arab Emirates","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Zayed University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammad Amin","key":"kuhailpau","last":"Kuhail","name":"Kuhail, Mohammad Amin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"lauesenpau","last":"Lauesen","locid":"ea6d10cf-6bb5-4414-8966-f1ed2591f794","name":"Lauesen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-2300-6934","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/access.2020.3002591","issn":["21693536"],"journal":"IEEE Access","pages":"110264-110278","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"IEEE Access","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087402232"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4f38ee1b-a4e6-4929-86fb-8baaa54b7d34"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Uvis: A Formula-Based End-User Tool for Data Visualization","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382454","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"We have known for decades that IT projects often fail. The usual explanation is that the cause is poor project management, poor cost estimation, poor requirements, etc. But how can we prevent these causes? To answer this question, it is not sufficient to know that there was poor project management, etc. Would it suffice to educate better project managers? And what would we have to teach them that they don't learn today? We have to know what actually took place in the projects, identify the root causes, and find ways to prevent them (cures). This is similar to accident investigations in aviation. This paper reports the results of five accident investigations of large government IT projects in Denmark. We identified 37 root causes and 22 potential cures. Surprisingly, only one of the causes is programming-related. Each project suffered from around 15 of the causes. Twenty-seven of the causes are not reported in the research literature on IT project failures (e.g. surprises with system integration and wrong estimate of human performance). Half of the cures are familiar to developers, but were ignored in the specific project (example: usability test). The rest are unfamiliar (e.g. problem-oriented requirements and monitoring remaining work).","author_count":1,"contributors":["Lauesen, Søren"],"cuid":["S02-099.37-038331"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","class":"merged","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Accident prevention","Project failure","Project management","Software development"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"it project failures causes and cures","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2020.2986545","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.37-038331","identifier":[{"id":"85084330379","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-77a7202b-c0fe-4024-9699-9b3be71db48e","itu-d05a4fb5-8de5-406a-9757-70ec099e4f6a"],"keyword":["Project management","accident prevention","project failure","software development"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E197C9E32D359375148052BF5F1D9CC2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85351745/Damages.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2020.2986545","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9060941","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"lauesenpau","last":"Lauesen","locid":"ea6d10cf-6bb5-4414-8966-f1ed2591f794","name":"Lauesen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-2300-6934","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/access.2020.2986545","issn":["21693536"],"journal":"IEEE Access","paperid":"//doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2020.2986545","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"IEEE Access","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85084330379"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-77a7202b-c0fe-4024-9699-9b3be71db48e","itu-d05a4fb5-8de5-406a-9757-70ec099e4f6a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"IT Project Failures, Causes and Cures","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.37-038331","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: When localised scleroderma occurs in the face, neck and scalp area, it is called scleroderma en coup de sabre (SCS) for its resemblance to the stroke of a sabre. Most observed characteristics: abnormal skin and dental development, facial atrophy and neurological complications. The aim was to evaluate the extent of SCS in the underlying subcutis, including teeth/bone tissues. The goal was to solve, how far the external visual skin abnormality extends in depth, and if the condition appears within and limited to craniofacial neural crest fields. METHODS: Photographic and radiographic materials from six patients (one male, five females, aged 5-39 years) were included. The cases were divided in three groups, two in each, according to similarity in location of SCS in the skin. Dentition and gingiva were analysed clinically and from intra-oral photos, dental radiographs and orthopantomograms. Agenesis, dental maturity stage (root length), deviation in crown and root morphology (size and shape), and eruption disturbances were registered. Profile and frontal radiographs were analysed cephalometrically for jaw relationships and bone structures. RESULTS: In SCS, skin affection corresponds to the neural crest regions/fields. A close spatial association between skin, teeth and bone affections within neural crest fields was found. No common traits in profile analyses were observed. Asymmetry from minor to severe appears in the frontal analyses. A malformation in planum sphenoidale was observed in two individuals with the same location of skin affections. CONCLUSION: SCS conditions seem to extend from the skin in the depth to the sella turcica area within neural crest fields.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Lauesen, Søren Rødsgaard","Daugaard-Jensen, J.","Lauridsen, E. F.","Kjær, Inger"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-481291"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"localised scleroderma en coup de sabre affecting the skin dentition and bone tissue within craniofacial neural crest fields clinical and radiographic study of six patients","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-481291","identifier":[{"id":"30847683","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85065023311","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-930cfda8-5758-4247-9b19-b1281ebf9165"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4262B6762B14A698387A0C9D480ECA16"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Odontology, Section 02 - Paediatric Dentistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"S. R.","key":"lauesenpau","last":"Lauesen","locid":"b76a2c3d-090c-4473-8eee-c61a1fa2e2d9","name":"Lauesen, Søren Rødsgaard","name_org":"Lauesen, S. R.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"J.","key":"daugaardjensenpau","last":"Daugaard-Jensen","name":"Daugaard-Jensen, J.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"E. F.","key":"lauridsenpau","last":"Lauridsen","name":"Lauridsen, E. F.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"I.","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"c90dedb9-cbeb-4b52-ab87-8cc660ab2339","name":"Kjær, Inger","name_org":"Kjær, I.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30847683"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s40368-019-00427-7","issn":["18186300","19969805"],"issn_org":["18186300"],"issue":"4","journal":"European Archives of Paediatric Dentistry","pages":"339-350","status":"p","title":"European Archives of Paediatric Dentistry","title_org":"European archives of paediatric dentistry : official journal of the European Academy of Paediatric Dentistry","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85065023311"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-930cfda8-5758-4247-9b19-b1281ebf9165"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Localised scleroderma en coup de sabre affecting the skin, dentition and bone tissue within craniofacial neural crest fields : clinical and radiographic study of six patients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-481291","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"IT developers and consultants often ask for an exemplary requirements specification as a starting point for their own project. Problem-oriented requirements SL-07 is such a specification. It is a template filled out with a complex example: Requirements for an Electronic Health Record system (EHR). There is a matching contract.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Lauesen, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382586"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Agile development","Software requirements","tender process"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"problemorienterede krav sl 000000000007 vejledning og kontrakt v000000000006","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://www.itu.dk/people/slauesen/SorenReqs.html","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382586","ids":["itu-58bb0c12-1e86-4c16-a8f4-e04bfa72ea1d"],"keyword":["Software requirements","agile development","tender process"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-426BA58CB34AA9001ED3BF37B003E629"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://www.itu.dk/people/slauesen/SorenReqs.html","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"lauesenpau","last":"Lauesen","locid":"ea6d10cf-6bb5-4414-8966-f1ed2591f794","name":"Lauesen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-2300-6934","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"edition":"6","isbn":["9781790662975"],"pages":"128","publisher":"Amazon Kindle","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-58bb0c12-1e86-4c16-a8f4-e04bfa72ea1d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Problemorienterede krav SL-07 : Vejledning og kontrakt v6","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382586","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"[Context and motivation] Traditional requirements describe what the system shall do. This gives suppliers little freedom to use what they have already. In contrast, problem-oriented requirements describe the customer’s demands: what he wants to use the system for and which problems he wants to remove. The supplier specifies how his system will deal with these issues. The author developed the problem-oriented approach in 2007 on request from the Danish Government, and named it SL-07. [Question/problem] SL-07 has been used in many projects – usually with success. However, we had no detailed re¬ports of the effects. [Princi¬pal ideas/results] This paper is a case study of SL-07 in acquisition of a complex case-management system. The author wrote the requirements and managed the supplier selection. Next, he was asked to run the entire acquisition project, although he was a novice project manager. Some of the results were: The problem-oriented requirements were a factor 5 shorter than traditional requirements in the same domain. Stakeholders understood them and identified missing demands. Suppliers could write excellent proposals with a modest effort. The requirements were a good basis for writing test cases and resolving conflicts during development. The delivery was 9 months late, but this was not related to the requirements. [Contribution] This is a publication of a full, real-life, complex requirements specification, the selection document, error lists, etc. The full texts are available on the author’s web-site. The paper discusses the results and illustrates them with samples from the full texts.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Lauesen, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381986"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["COTS","Case study","SL 07","Small enterprises","problem oriented requirements","supplier selction","usability requirements"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"problem oriented requirements in practice a case study","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83000910/ProblemOrientedReqs5.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381986","identifier":[{"id":"85043396745","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-31031e8a-68dc-4f3f-ad48-3509b15fcfa8"],"keyword":["COTS","SL-07","case study","problem-oriented requirements","small enterprises","supplier selction","usability requirements"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3B786FE86ADA5C6CEB2C2E25415B39D9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83000910/ProblemOrientedReqs5.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"lauesenpau","last":"Lauesen","locid":"ea6d10cf-6bb5-4414-8966-f1ed2591f794","name":"Lauesen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-2300-6934","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-77243-1_1","eisbn":["9783319772431"],"isbn":["9783319772424"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"3-19","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"24th International Working Conference, REFSQ 2018 Utrecht, The Netherlands, March 19–22, 2018 Proceedings","title":"Requirements Engineering: Foundation for Software Quality"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85043396745"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-31031e8a-68dc-4f3f-ad48-3509b15fcfa8"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Problem-Oriented Requirements in Practice : A case study","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381986","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"IT developers and consultants often ask for an exemplary requirements specification as a starting point for their own project. Problem-oriented requirements SL-07 is such a specification. It is a template filled out with a complex example: Requirements for an Electronic Health Record system (EHR). This version has a matching contract, new selection criteria, requirements to the Development process, etc.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Lauesen, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382014"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Agile development","Software requirements","tender process"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"problem oriented requirements sl 000000000007 guide and contract v000000000006","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://www.itu.dk/people/slauesen/SorenReqs.html","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382014","ids":["itu-332a37a2-918c-45f6-a5d2-25427c91ad6b"],"keyword":["Software requirements","agile development","tender process"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A001D4CDFC363FC273183875E5D72056"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://www.itu.dk/people/slauesen/SorenReqs.html","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"lauesenpau","last":"Lauesen","locid":"ea6d10cf-6bb5-4414-8966-f1ed2591f794","name":"Lauesen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-2300-6934","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781791748906"],"pages":"128","publisher":"Amazon Kindle","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-332a37a2-918c-45f6-a5d2-25427c91ad6b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Problem-oriented requirements SL-07 : Guide and contract v6","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382014","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"This booklet contains a software requirements specification for a complex system - and a guide to why it is written in this way. The specification itself can be used as inspiration and template for other systems. Until now it has been used successfully in 100+ projects ranging from public acquisitions to product development and agile in-house projects.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Lauesen, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382016"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Agile development","Complex systems","Public Acquisitions","Software Requirements Specification","Template Usage"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"guide to requirements sl 000000000007 version 000000000005 problem oriented requirements v000000000005","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.itu.dk/people/slauesen/Papers/RequirementsGuideSL-07v5-online.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382016","ids":["itu-333f5b36-fe3b-4ad6-a9b7-420dded2fdef"],"keyword":["Agile Development","Complex Systems","Public Acquisitions","Software Requirements Specification","Template Usage"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-392386041347FDA77B5D2F84CC863A41"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"lauesenpau","last":"Lauesen","locid":"ea6d10cf-6bb5-4414-8966-f1ed2591f794","name":"Lauesen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-2300-6934","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"edition":"5","isbn":["9781523320240"],"pages":"107","publisher":"Lauesen Publishing","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-333f5b36-fe3b-4ad6-a9b7-420dded2fdef"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Guide to Requirements SL-07 version 5 : Problem-oriented requirements v5","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382016","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"A health record database contains structured data fields that identify the patient, such as patient ID, patient name, e-mail and phone number. These data are fairly easy to de-identify, that is, replace with other identifiers. However, these data also occur in fields with doctors’ free-text notes written in an abbreviated style that cannot be analyzed grammatically. If we replace a word that looks like a name, but isn’t, we degrade readability and medical correctness. If we fail to replace it when we should, we degrade confidentiality. We de-identified an existing Danish electronic health record database, ending up with 323,122 patient health records. We had to invent many methods for de-identifying potential identifiers in the free-text notes. The de-identified health records should be used with caution for statistical purposes because we removed health records that were so special that they couldn’t be de-identified. Furthermore, we distorted geography by replacing zip codes with random zip codes.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Pantazos, Kostas","Lauesen, Søren","Lippert, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383061"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Anonymi","Consistency","De identification","Electronic health record","Readability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"preserving medical correctness readability and consistency in de identified health records","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82419149/Preserving_v2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383061","identifier":[{"id":"85034637745","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-79eb628b-a91d-43cf-b81c-e74f045a7cb5"],"keyword":["anonymi","consistency","de-identification","electronic health record","readability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-831CE893722BA62DA181E8226CAEBE4F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82419149/Preserving_v2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kostas","key":"pantazospau","last":"Pantazos","name":"Pantazos, Kostas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"lauesenpau","last":"Lauesen","locid":"ea6d10cf-6bb5-4414-8966-f1ed2591f794","name":"Lauesen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-2300-6934","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"lippertpau","last":"Lippert","name":"Lippert, Søren","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/1460458216647760","issn":["14604582","17412811"],"issn_org":["14604582"],"journal":"Health Informatics Journal","pages":"1-13","publisher":"Sage Publishing","status":"p","title":"Health Informatics Journal"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85034637745"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-79eb628b-a91d-43cf-b81c-e74f045a7cb5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Preserving medical correctness, readability and consistency in de-identified health records","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383061","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"In this article the authors investigated a visualization tool (uVis) for end-user developers, in order to see how end users actually use it. The tool was an early version and the investigation helped the authors to improve it. The investigation showed that users appreciated the simple formula language, the coordinated panels, and the drag-and-drop mechanism. However, the most important thing for them was the immediate response when they changed something, for instance part of a formula. The entire visualization was updated immediately without having to switch from development view to production view. With uVis, developers construct a visualization from simple visual components such as boxes, curvePoints, and textboxes. All component properties such as Top and BackColor can be complex formulas similar to spreadsheet formulas. The operands in the formula can address relational data in a database, other visual objects, and dialog data provided by the user. A special Rows property can bind to a database query and make the component replicate itself for each row in the query. In this way, traditional as well as novel visualizations can be constructed. The most serious usability problems were data binding and not noticing errors (errors were shown in an error list, but not in the formula that had the error). There were many other usability problems. Removing them would speed up learning and make the tool more successful.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Lauesen, Søren","Pantazos, Kostas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381413"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Data visualization","Usability","end user tool"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"end user development of visualizations","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2352/J.ImagingSci.Technol.2016.60.1.010408","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381413","identifier":[{"id":"84958720831","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-0aab9f10-b456-4463-a87d-2175a9a66d5f"],"keyword":["data visualization","end-user tool","usability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-A0472B29315722FDF70B4469D8BA4C46"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2352/J.ImagingSci.Technol.2016.60.1.010408","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82437053/EndUserViz_2016.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"lauesenpau","last":"Lauesen","locid":"ea6d10cf-6bb5-4414-8966-f1ed2591f794","name":"Lauesen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-2300-6934","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kostas","key":"pantazospau","last":"Pantazos","name":"Pantazos, Kostas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.2352/j.imagingsci.technol.2016.60.1.010408","issn":["10623701","19433522"],"issn_org":["10623701"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Imaging Science and Technology","publisher":"Society for Imaging Science and Technology","status":"p","title":"Journal of Imaging Science and Technology","title_org":"The Journal of Imaging Science and Technology","volume":"60"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84958720831"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0aab9f10-b456-4463-a87d-2175a9a66d5f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"End-User Development of Visualizations","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381413","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Psoriasis is a chronic cutaneous inflammatory disease. The immunopathogenesis is a complex interplay between T cells, dendritic cells and the epidermis in which T cells and dendritic cells maintain skin inflammation. Anti-tumour necrosis factor (anti-TNF)-α agents have been approved for therapeutic use across a range of inflammatory disorders including psoriasis, but the anti-inflammatory mechanisms of anti-TNF-α in lesional psoriatic skin are not fully understood. We investigated early events in skin from psoriasis patients after treatment with anti-TNF-α antibodies by use of bioinformatics tools. We used the Human Gene 1.0 ST Array to analyse gene expression in punch biopsies taken from psoriatic patients before and also 4 and 14 days after initiation of treatment with the anti-TNF-α agent adalimumab. The gene expression was analysed by gene set enrichment analysis using the Functional Annotation Tool from DAVID Bioinformatics Resources. The most enriched pathway was visualised by the Pathview Package on Kyoto Encyclopedia of Genes and Genomes (KEGG) graphs. The analysis revealed new very early events in psoriasis after adalimumab treatment. Some of these events have been described after longer periods of anti-TNF-α treatment when clinical and histological changes appear, suggesting that effects of anti-TNF-α treatment on gene expression appear very early before clinical and histological changes. Combining microarray data on biopsies from psoriasis patients with pathway analysis allowed us to integrate in vitro findings into the identification of mechanisms that may be important in vivo. Furthermore, these results may reflect primary effect of anti-TNF-α treatment in contrast to studies of gene expression changes following clinical and histological changes, which may reflect secondary changes correlated to the healing of the skin.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nielsen, Ane Langkilde-Lauesen","Olsen, Lene C.","Saetrom, Pål","Drabløs, Finn","Besenbacher, Søren","Raaby, Line","Johansen, Claus","Iversen, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-244398"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Norwegian University of Science and Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pathway analysis of skin from psoriasis patients after adalimumab treatment reveals new early events in the anti inflammatory mechanism of anti tnf α","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5179238/pdf/pone.0167437.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-244398","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5179238","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85007316404","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28005985","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-c975296d-dc63-48e3-8695-94bc7d1ff3eb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-56534A4C273F4570F04D85096B0A9938"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5179238/pdf/pone.0167437.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Dermatology and Venereology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"norwegian university of science and technology","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian University of Science and Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ane Langkilde-Lauesen","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"0617cbaf-1771-447c-8ffe-c3b0ad8ed0d8","name":"Nielsen, Ane Langkilde-Lauesen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene C.","key":"olsenoth","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, Lene C.","rank":2,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pål","key":"saetromoth","last":"Saetrom","name":"Saetrom, Pål","rank":3,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Finn","key":"drabløsoth","last":"Drabløs","name":"Drabløs, Finn","rank":4,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"besenbacheroth","last":"Besenbacher","locid":"ce64758a-054a-40ca-897b-543899af8c0f","name":"Besenbacher, Søren","rank":5,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Raaby","key":"steenbergoth","last":"Steenberg","locid":"47a1c989-3031-450d-8d06-995b987ef525","name":"Raaby, Line","name_org":"Steenberg, Line Raaby","rank":6,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus","key":"johansenoth","last":"Johansen","locid":"593a3337-e8ac-482a-ace2-f36521834d3c","name":"Johansen, Claus","orcid":"0000-0002-5665-5212","rank":7,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"iversenoth","last":"Iversen","locid":"0ee9531c-28fa-41bc-8eb4-64d8ae7f0fb1","name":"Iversen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-1816-4508","rank":8,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"}],"pmid":["28005985"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0167437","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"12","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e0167437","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","title_org":"P L o S One","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85007316404"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c975296d-dc63-48e3-8695-94bc7d1ff3eb"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Pathway Analysis of Skin from Psoriasis Patients after Adalimumab Treatment Reveals New Early Events in the Anti-Inflammatory Mechanism of Anti-TNF-α","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-244398","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Linear scleroderma en coup de sabre (SCS) is a rare skin condition, where dense collagen is deposited in a localised groove of the head and neck area resembling the stroke of a sabre. The SCS may involve the oral cavity, but the severity and relation to this skin abnormality is unknown. A paediatric dentist may be the first medical person to identify SCS by its involvement in dentition. It is assumed that the malformation of a dentition could be associated with the severity of the skin deviation. CASE REPORT: A 6-year and 10-month-old Turkish girl with a history of SCS was referred for dental diagnostics and treatment. The SCS skin lesion affected the left side of her hairline over the forehead and nose, involving the left orbit proceeding towards the left oral region. Dental clinical/radiographic examination revealed malformed left maxillary incisors with short roots and lack of eruption. FOLLOW-UP: The patient has been regularly controlled and treated since she was first diagnosed. A surgical and orthodontic treatment was performed to ensure optimal occlusion, space and alveolar bone development. The present age of the patient is 14 years and 10 months. CONCLUSION: This case demonstrated a patient with a left-sided skin defect (SCS) and a left-sided local malformation in her dentition. It is possible that there is a developmental connection between these two left-sided defects, both with an ectodermal origin.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hørberg, M","Lauesen, Søren Rødsgaard","Daugaard-Jensen, J","Kjær, Inger"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-516277"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"linear scleroderma en coup de sabre including abnormal dental development","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-516277","identifier":[{"id":"25355303","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84925748252","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-cdaa5209-88e3-48cf-abca-ee6f6689c8dd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0A5C2623B83D92CA34E1894FBCC77951"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Odontology, Postgraduate Programme in Orthodontics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"M","key":"hørbergpau","last":"Hørberg","name":"Hørberg, M","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"S R","key":"lauesenpau","last":"Lauesen","locid":"b76a2c3d-090c-4473-8eee-c61a1fa2e2d9","name":"Lauesen, Søren Rødsgaard","name_org":"Lauesen, S R","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"J","key":"daugaardjensenpau","last":"Daugaard-Jensen","name":"Daugaard-Jensen, J","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"I","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"c90dedb9-cbeb-4b52-ab87-8cc660ab2339","name":"Kjær, Inger","name_org":"Kjær, I","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25355303"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s40368-014-0148-6","issn":["18186300","19969805"],"issn_org":["18186300"],"issue":"2","journal":"European Archives of Paediatric Dentistry","pages":"227-231","status":"p","title":"European Archives of Paediatric Dentistry","title_org":"European archives of paediatric dentistry","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84925748252"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cdaa5209-88e3-48cf-abca-ee6f6689c8dd"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Linear scleroderma en coup de sabre including abnormal dental development","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-516277","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"A toolkit facilitates the visualization development process. The process can be further enhanced by integrating the toolkits in development environments. This paper describes how the uVis toolkit, a formula-based visualiza- tion toolkit, has been extended with a development environment, called uVis Studio. Instead of programming, developers apply a Drag-Drop-Set-View-Interact approach. Developers bind controls to data, and the Studio gives immediate visual feedback in the Design Panel. This is a novel feature, called What-You-Bind-Is-What- You-Get. The Studio also provides Modes that allow developers to interact and view the visualization from the end-user's perspective without switching workspace, and Auto-Completion; a feature of the Property Grid that provides suggestions not only for the formula language syntax but also for the tables, the table elds and the relationships in the database. We conducted a usability study with six developers to evaluate if the Studio and its features enhance cognition and facilitate the visualization development. The results show that developers appreciated the Drag-Drop-Set- View-Interact approach, the What-You-Bind-Is-What-You-Get, the Auto-Completion and the Modes. Several usability problems were identified, and some suggestions for improvement include: new panels, better presentation of the Modes, and better error messages. © (2013) COPYRIGHT Society of Photo-Optical Instrumentation Engineers (SPIE). Downloading of the abstract is permitted for personal use only.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Pantazos, Kostas","Kuhail, Mohammad Amin","Lauesen, Søren","Xu, Shangjin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-282281"],"event":{"end":"2013-02-06","place":"Burlingame, CA, us","start":"2013-02-04","title":"Visualization and Data Analysis 2013","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Computer Programming","Databases","Feedback","Visualization"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"uvis studio an integrated development environment for visualization","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-282281","ids":["cbs-48ac8a61-aa82-496b-b55b-a08d4861610f"],"keyword":["Computer programming","Databases","Feedback","Visualization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-35A3029D6907E2F622F06436C51C50D9"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of IT Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kostas","key":"pantazospau","last":"Pantazos","locid":"fc9298d6-557b-4f3c-a005-7bed5d0cbe87","name":"Pantazos, Kostas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammad Amin","key":"kuhailpau","last":"Kuhail","name":"Kuhail, Mohammad Amin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"lauesenpau","last":"Lauesen","name":"Lauesen, Søren","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Shangjin","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Shangjin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Pak Chung","key":"wongpedh","last":"Wong","name":"Wong, Pak Chung","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"David L.","key":"kaopedh","last":"Kao","name":"Kao, David L.","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ming C.","key":"haopedh","last":"Hao","name":"Hao, Ming C.","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Chaomei","key":"chenpedh","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Chaomei","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9780819494276"],"issn":["0277786X"],"pages":"15-30","place":"Bellingham, WA","publisher":"SPIE - International Society for Optical Engineering","series":"Proceedings of SPIE - International Society for Optical Engineering","status":"p","title":"Visualization and Data Analysis 2013"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84875842341"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-48ac8a61-aa82-496b-b55b-a08d4861610f"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"uVis Studio : An Integrated Development Environment for Visualization","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-282281","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Abstract Objective: To compare the root development and the growth rate of the mandibular third molar (M3 inf) in individuals where the M3 inf erupted vs individuals exhibiting M3 inf impaction. Materials and Methods: Serial standardized intraoral radiographs (Eggen technique) were taken annually of the mandibular third molar region from 132 subjects (71 male and 61 female) from 15 to 20 years of age. Based on the films, 264 lower third molars were classified into an eruption and an impaction group. Root development was recorded according to a quantitative method described by Haavikko (1970), and the eruption status was analyzed using logistic regression. Results: In total, 155 (59%) of the M3 inf erupted, and 109 (41%) were impacted at age 20. In 44 (33%) patients both M3 inf were impacted, in 21 (16%) patients one tooth was erupted and the contralateral tooth impacted, and in 67 (51%) patients both M3 inf were erupted. The more mature a tooth was at age 15, the higher was the probability of eruption (odds ratio: 3.89, P <.001). The growth rate of the root development stage was statistically significantly associated with the probability of eruption (odds ratio: 10.50, P ¿=¿ .041). Conclusions: Delayed mandibular third molar root development is associated with impaction. Radiographs taken at age 15 may predict the risk of impaction and thereby guide decision making for the orthodontist or the oral and maxillofacial surgeon.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Lauesen, Søren Rødsgaard","Andreasen, Jens Ove","Gerds, Thomas Alexander","Christensen, Søren Steno Ahrensburg","Borum, Mette","Hillerup, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-434363"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association between third mandibular molar impaction and degree of root development in adolescents","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2319/102911-667.1","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-434363","identifier":[{"id":"22702958","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84872006190","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-44843b2b-4af1-4511-a837-4ab3865eac5f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5CC78C072A76CDF90C15CFDE00FCE641"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2319/102911-667.1","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Odontology, Postgraduate Programme in Orthodontics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Søren Rødsgaard","key":"lauesenpau","last":"Lauesen","locid":"b76a2c3d-090c-4473-8eee-c61a1fa2e2d9","name":"Lauesen, Søren Rødsgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens O","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"c523b763-f9d6-4436-9feb-f9c8027437cd","name":"Andreasen, Jens Ove","name_org":"Andreasen, Jens O","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Thomas Alexander","key":"gerdspau","last":"Gerds","locid":"b87ed711-194a-48dc-b83a-3c7aad18a00d","name":"Gerds, Thomas Alexander","orcid":"0000-0002-5955-816X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren Steno Ahrensburg","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"aa43c90b-6db4-4c62-b5e5-f89fd6c2c0e3","name":"Christensen, Søren Steno Ahrensburg","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mette","key":"borumpau","last":"Borum","name":"Borum, Mette","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren","key":"hilleruppau","last":"Hillerup","locid":"f1d43760-6113-4db1-b7bb-e003c91bada4","name":"Hillerup, Søren","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22702958"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2319/102911-667.1","issn":["00033219","19457103"],"issue":"1","journal":"The Angle Orthodontist","pages":"3-9","status":"p","title":"The Angle Orthodontist","volume":"83"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84872006190"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-44843b2b-4af1-4511-a837-4ab3865eac5f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Association between third mandibular molar impaction and degree of root development in adolescents","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-434363","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Existing custom visualization tools provide cognitive artefacts that can reduce the cognitive barriers designers encounter in visual mapping, mapping data to visual primitives (e.g. ellipse, rectangle) and their properties (e.g. colour, size.) However, our experience with designers shows that the existing artefacts are insufficient. In particular, designers struggle to understand the relationship between visual primitives, their properties, and data. Moreover, it is hard to verify the correctness of the visual mappings. In response, we developed a new cognitive artefact, the inspector, that explicitly shows the data behind visual primitive and their properties. We evaluated the impact of the inspector on usability with seven designers. The result shows that the inspector reduced usability problems and helped designers verify the visual mappings.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Kuhail, Mohammad A.","Lauesen, Søren","Pantazos, Kostas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-288171"],"event":{"end":"2013-02-24","place":"Barcelona, es","start":"2013-02-21","title":"The 4th International Conference on Information Visualization Theory and Applications. IVAPP 2013","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Visual mapping"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the inspector a cognitive artefact for visual mapping","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-288171","ids":["cbs-864fb0e6-4701-495d-bda2-ce51c5edb305"],"keyword":["Cognitive Artefacts","Custom Visualizations","Information Visualization Tools","Inspector","Visual Mapping"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-CA724C2E2B546298706C4B8D81E13DCA"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of IT Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammad A.","key":"kuhailpau","last":"Kuhail","name":"Kuhail, Mohammad A.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"lauesenpau","last":"Lauesen","name":"Lauesen, Søren","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kostas","key":"pantazospau","last":"Pantazos","locid":"fc9298d6-557b-4f3c-a005-7bed5d0cbe87","name":"Pantazos, Kostas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sabine","key":"coquillartpedh","last":"Coquillart","name":"Coquillart, Sabine","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Carlos","key":"andujarpedh","last":"Andujar","name":"Andujar, Carlos","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Robert S.","key":"larameepedh","last":"Laramee","name":"Laramee, Robert S.","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Andreas","key":"kerrenpedh","last":"Kerren","name":"Kerren, Andreas","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"José","key":"brazpedh","last":"Braz","name":"Braz, José","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9789898565464"],"pages":"525-534","place":"Setubal","publisher":"SCITEPRESS Digital Library","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the International Conference on Computer Graphics Theory and Applications (GRAPP 2013) and International Conference on Information Visualization Theory and Applications (IVAPP 2013)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84878133111"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-864fb0e6-4701-495d-bda2-ce51c5edb305"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"The Inspector : A Cognitive Artefact for Visual Mapping","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-288171","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"This paper investigates End-User Development of Information Visualization. More specifically, we investigated how existing visualization tools allow end-user developers to construct visualizations. End-user developers have some developing or scripting skills to perform relatively advanced tasks such as data manipulation, but no formal training in programming. 18 visualization tools were surveyed from an enduser developer perspective. The results of this survey study show that end-user developers need better tools to create and modify custom visualizations. A closer collaboration between End-User Development and Information Visualization researchers could contribute towards the development of better tools to support custom visualizations. In addition, as empirical evaluations of these tools are lacking both research communities should focus more on this aspect. The study serves as a starting point towards the engagement of end-user developers in visualization development.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Pantazos, Kostas","Lauesen, Søren","Vatrapu, Ravi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-290259"],"event":{"end":"2013-06-13","place":"Copenhagen , dk","start":"2013-06-10","title":"The 4th International Symposium, IS-EUD 2013","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["End User Development","Information visualization","Visualization Tools"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"end user development of information visualization","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-290259","identifier":[{"id":"84884379175","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-9bc1a711-0bd0-4f63-be24-52505bc8f69f"],"keyword":["End-User Development","Information Visualization","Visualization Tools"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DF0B48E7AC25428E395C0527E5473946"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of IT Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kostas","key":"pantazospau","last":"Pantazos","locid":"fc9298d6-557b-4f3c-a005-7bed5d0cbe87","name":"Pantazos, Kostas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"lauesenpau","last":"Lauesen","name":"Lauesen, Søren","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ravi","key":"vatrapupau","last":"Vatrapu","locid":"93ba7069-df22-46b2-bf4f-5eb53175ef75","name":"Vatrapu, Ravi","orcid":"0000-0002-9109-5281","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpedh","last":"Dittrich","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Margaret","key":"burnettpedh","last":"Burnett","name":"Burnett, Margaret","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders","key":"mørchpedh","last":"Mørch","name":"Mørch, Anders","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"David","key":"redmilespedh","last":"Redmiles","name":"Redmiles, David","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-642-38706-7_9","eisbn":["9783642387067"],"isbn":["9783642387050"],"issn":["03029743"],"issue":"7897","pages":"104-119","place":"Heidelberg","publisher":"Springer Science+Business Media","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"End-User Development 4th International Symposium, IS-EUD 2013, Copenhagen, Denmark, June 10-13, 2013. Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84884379175"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-9bc1a711-0bd0-4f63-be24-52505bc8f69f"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"End-User Development of Information Visualization","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-290259","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Most commercial visualization tools support an easy and quick creation of conventional time-oriented visualizations such as line charts, but customization is limited. In contrast, some academic visualization tools and programming languages support the creation of some customizable time-oriented visualizations but it is time consuming and hard. To combine efficiency, the effort required to develop a visualization, and customizability, the ability to tailor a visualization, we developed time-oriented building blocks that address the specifics of time (e.g. linear vs. cyclic or point-based vs. interval-based) and consist of inner customizable parts (e.g. ticks). A combination of the time-oriented and other primitive graphical building blocks allowed the creation of several customizable advanced time-oriented visualizations. The appearance and behavior of the blocks are specified using spreadsheet-like formulas. We compared our approach with other popular visualization tools. Evaluation showed that our approach rates well in customizability.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Kuhail, Mohammad Amin","Pantazos, Kostas","Lauesen, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384462"],"event":{"end":"2012-07-18","place":"Rethymnon, gr","start":"2012-07-16","title":"8th International Symposium on Visual Computing","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Building blocks","Customization","Spreadsheet like Formulas","graphical primitives","time oriented visualizations"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"customizable time oriented visualizations","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://itu.dk/people/moak/Papers/Customizable-Time-Oriented-Visualizations_Final.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384462","identifier":[{"id":"84866696535","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-d8eb1e8f-538f-43f2-97bb-b232646290d2"],"keyword":["building blocks","customization","graphical primitives","spreadsheet-like formulas","time-oriented visualizations"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8854E3E19DAD5F9445934A49684488B0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://itu.dk/people/moak/Papers/Customizable-Time-Oriented-Visualizations_Final.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammad Amin","key":"kuhailpau","last":"Kuhail","name":"Kuhail, Mohammad Amin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kostas","key":"pantazospau","last":"Pantazos","name":"Pantazos, Kostas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"lauesenpau","last":"Lauesen","locid":"ea6d10cf-6bb5-4414-8966-f1ed2591f794","name":"Lauesen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-2300-6934","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["03029743","16113349"],"issn_org":["03029743"],"journal":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","volume":"7432"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84866696535"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d8eb1e8f-538f-43f2-97bb-b232646290d2"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Customizable Time-Oriented Visualizations","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384462","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"One approach to visualization construction is to use complex blocks (widgets) that are tailored for specific visualizations, and customize the visualizations by setting the properties of the widgets. This approach allows fast and easy visualization construction but falls short if the user wants different appearance or behavior than what the widgets support. Another approach is to combine primitive graphical elements using traditional programming or visualization toolkits. Traditional programming allows high customizability, but it is time consuming and hard to develop advanced visualizations. Visualization toolkits allow easier visualization creation in some cases, but customization and interaction are tedious. As an alternative, we developed uVis visualization tool that uses spreadsheet-like formulas to connect building blocks. uVis formulas can refer to building blocks and database tables. We created several advanced visualizations, and compared our approach against others. Evaluation shows that our approach improved customizability.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Kuhail, Mohammad Amin","Lauesen, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383785"],"event":{"end":"2012-02-26","place":"Rome, it","start":"2012-02-24","title":"International Conference on Information Visualization Theory and Applications","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Customizable Widgets","Primitive Graphical Elements","Spreadsheet like Formulas","Visualization Construction","Visualization toolkits"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"customizable visualizations with formula linked building blocks","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://itu.dk/people/moak/Papers/CUSTOMIZABLE%20VISUALIZATIONS%20WITH%20FORMULA-LINKED%20BUILDING%20BLOCKS_Final.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383785","identifier":[{"id":"84862225072","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ad7fe37d-c52d-4f19-a03c-31279493405d"],"keyword":["Customizable Widgets","Primitive Graphical Elements","Spreadsheet-like Formulas","Visualization Construction","Visualization Toolkits"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-940437858CAF54850CDB3014D8FDED15"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://itu.dk/people/moak/Papers/CUSTOMIZABLE%20VISUALIZATIONS%20WITH%20FORMULA-LINKED%20BUILDING%20BLOCKS_Final.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.ivapp.visigrapp.org/Abstracts/2012/IVAPP_2012_Abstracts.htm","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammad Amin","key":"kuhailpau","last":"Kuhail","name":"Kuhail, Mohammad Amin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"lauesenpau","last":"Lauesen","locid":"ea6d10cf-6bb5-4414-8966-f1ed2591f794","name":"Lauesen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-2300-6934","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ad7fe37d-c52d-4f19-a03c-31279493405d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Customizable Visualizations with Formula-Linked Building Blocks","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383785","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Abstract. [Context and motivation] Use cases are widely used as a substantial part of requirements, also when little programming is expected (COTS-based systems). [Question/problem] Are use cases effective as requirements? To an-swer this question, we invited professionals and researchers to specify require-ments for the same project: Acquire a new system to support a hotline. [Princi-pal ideas/results] Among the 15 replies, eight used traditional use cases that specified a dialog between users and system. Seven used a related technique, task description, which specified the customer's needs without specifying a dialog. [Contribution] It turned out that the traditional use cases covered the customer's needs poorly in areas where improvement was important but diffi-cult. Use cases also restricted the solution space severely. Tasks didn't have these problems and allowed an easy comparison of solutions.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Lauesen, Søren","Kuhail, Mohammad Amin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382381"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["COTS Based Systems","Requirements specification","Solution Space Restriction","Task Descriptions","Use cases"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"use cases versus task descriptions","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/79953116205","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382381","identifier":[{"id":"79953116205","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-4ab54ee7-9924-4dcb-bdc8-c79e9cce5dc2"],"keyword":["COTS-Based Systems","Requirements Specification","Solution Space Restriction","Task Descriptions","Use Cases"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-055DC626440D01C46D5773CCBACFD605"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"lauesenpau","last":"Lauesen","locid":"ea6d10cf-6bb5-4414-8966-f1ed2591f794","name":"Lauesen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-2300-6934","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammad Amin","key":"kuhailpau","last":"Kuhail","name":"Kuhail, Mohammad Amin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["03029743","16113349"],"issn_org":["03029743"],"journal":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","pages":"106","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","volume":"D. Berry and X. Franch (Eds.): REFSQ 2011"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79953116205"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4ab54ee7-9924-4dcb-bdc8-c79e9cce5dc2"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Use cases versus task descriptions","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382381","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Abstract. Electronic health records (EHR) contain a large amount of structured data and free text. Exploring and sharing clinical data can improve healthcare and facilitate the development of medical software. However, revealing confidential information is against ethical principles and laws. We de-identified a Danish EHR database with 437,164 patients. The goal was to generate a version with real medical records, but related to artificial persons. We developed a de-identification algorithm that uses lists of named entities, simple language analysis, and special rules. Our algorithm consists of 3 steps: collect lists of identifiers from the database and external resources, define a replacement for each identifier, and replace identifiers in structured data and free text. Some patient records could not be safely de-identified, so the de-identified database has 323,122 patient records with an acceptable degree of anonymity, readability and correctness (F-measure of 95%). The algorithm has to be adjusted for each culture, language and database.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Lauesen, Søren","Pantazos, Kostas","Lippert, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382188"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Artificial persons","De identification","Electronic Health Records","Healthcare data privacy","Named entity recognition"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"de identifying an ehr database anonymity correctness and readability of the medical record","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/83055191218","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382188","identifier":[{"id":"83055191218","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-3e51b295-ec5d-45b1-9d29-fe80215d9054"],"keyword":["Artificial persons","De-identification","Electronic health records","Healthcare data privacy","Named entity recognition"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1EC05483D0308F813B0FB6D6D6A1B260"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"lauesenpau","last":"Lauesen","locid":"ea6d10cf-6bb5-4414-8966-f1ed2591f794","name":"Lauesen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-2300-6934","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kostas","key":"pantazospau","last":"Pantazos","name":"Pantazos, Kostas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"lippertpau","last":"Lippert","name":"Lippert, Søren","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09269630","18798365"],"issn_org":["09269630"],"journal":"Studies in Health Technology and Informatics","pages":"862-866","publisher":"IOS Press","status":"p","title":"Studies in Health Technology and Informatics","volume":"169"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-83055191218"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3e51b295-ec5d-45b1-9d29-fe80215d9054"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"De-identifying an EHR Database : Anonymity, Correctness and Readability of the Medical Record","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382188","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"IT developers and consultants often ask for an exemplary requirements specification as a starting point for their specific project. This document is the guide to such a specification, Requirements Template SL-07. The specification itself is a template filled out with a complex example: requirements for an Electronic Health Record system (EHR).","author_count":1,"contributors":["Lauesen, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384458"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Electronic Health Record system","IT project documentation","Requirements specification","Software engineering standards","Template SL 07"],"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"guide to requirements sl 000000000007 template with examples version 000000000002","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-384458","ids":["itu-d8a271c8-dc60-4433-a91b-451a3e688583"],"keyword":["Electronic Health Record system","IT project documentation","Requirements specification","Software engineering standards","Template SL-07"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8289B84D16C73259C05A6E14313EA378"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"lauesenpau","last":"Lauesen","locid":"ea6d10cf-6bb5-4414-8966-f1ed2591f794","name":"Lauesen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-2300-6934","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"edition":"version 2","isbn":["9788799234417"],"pages":"100","place":"Denmark","publisher":"Lauesen Publishing","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d8a271c8-dc60-4433-a91b-451a3e688583"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Guide to requirements SL-07 : Template with examples version 2","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384458","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Use cases are widely used as a substantial part of requirements, also when little programming is expected (COTS-based systems, Commercial-Off-The-Shelf). Are use cases effective as requirements? To answer this question, we invited professionals and researchers to specify requirements for the same project: Acquire a new system to support a hotline. Among the 15 replies, eight used traditional use cases that specified a dialog between user and system. Seven used a related technique, task description, which specified the customer’s needs without specifying a dialog. It also allowed the analyst to specify problem requirements—problems to be handled by the new system. It turned out that the traditional use cases covered the customer’s needs poorly in areas where improvement was important but difficult. Use cases also restricted the solution space severely. Tasks did not have these problems and allowed an easy comparison of solutions.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Lauesen, Søren","Kuhail, Mohammad Amin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383833"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Agile requirements","COTS","Diffusion of Innovation","Interaction design","Software requirements","Task description","Use case","Verification"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"task descriptions versus use cases","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/33312733/TaskDescriptionsDraftREJ.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-383833","ids":["itu-b025a0f0-e16d-4de7-91dd-53f3b89a20a5"],"keyword":["Agile requirements","COTS","Diffusion of innovation","Interaction design","Software requirements","Task description","Use case","Verification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CD4CE2DD8A4D6844C3662EAF5E3363A2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/33312733/TaskDescriptionsDraftREJ.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"lauesenpau","last":"Lauesen","locid":"ea6d10cf-6bb5-4414-8966-f1ed2591f794","name":"Lauesen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-2300-6934","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammad Amin","key":"kuhailpau","last":"Kuhail","name":"Kuhail, Mohammad Amin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09473602","1432010X"],"issn_org":["1432010X"],"issue":"DOI 10.1007/s00766-011-0140-1","journal":"Requirements Engineering","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Requirements Engineering","title_org":"Requirements Engineering (electronic edition)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84857369483"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b025a0f0-e16d-4de7-91dd-53f3b89a20a5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Task descriptions versus use cases","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383833","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Several tools use programming approaches for developing advanced visualizations. Others can with a few steps create simple visualizations with built-in patterns, and users with limited IT experience can use them. However, it is programming and time demanding to create and customize these visualizations. We introduce uVis, a tool that allows users with advanced spreadsheet-like IT knowledge and basic database understanding to create simple as well as advanced visualizations. These users construct visualizations by combining building blocks (i.e. controls, shapes). They specify spreadsheet-like formulas for color, position, interaction, etc. A formula can refer to database fields, other building blocks, properties, etc.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Pantazos, Kostas","Xu, Shangjin","Kuhail, Mohammad Amin","Lauesen, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384675"],"event":{"end":"2011-10-28","place":"Providence, RI, us","start":"2011-10-23","title":"IEEE VisWeek","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Building Blocks for Visualizations","Database Driven Visualizations","Spreadsheet like Formulas","User Friendly Visualizations","Visualization Tools"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"uvis a formula based visualization tool","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://visweek.org/visweek/2011/poster/visweek/infovis-uvis-formula-based-visualization-tool","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384675","ids":["itu-e74de4e6-42af-4ad7-b4bd-74aa322bfb99"],"keyword":["Building Blocks for Visualizations","Database-Driven Visualizations","Spreadsheet-Like Formulas","User-Friendly Visualizations","Visualization Tools"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-420964AC68B5C06CF1B941B069C63ECA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://visweek.org/visweek/2011/poster/visweek/infovis-uvis-formula-based-visualization-tool","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kostas","key":"pantazospau","last":"Pantazos","name":"Pantazos, Kostas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Shangjin","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Shangjin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammad Amin","key":"kuhailpau","last":"Kuhail","name":"Kuhail, Mohammad Amin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"lauesenpau","last":"Lauesen","locid":"ea6d10cf-6bb5-4414-8966-f1ed2591f794","name":"Lauesen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-2300-6934","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e74de4e6-42af-4ad7-b4bd-74aa322bfb99"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"uVis: A Formula-Based Visualization Tool","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384675","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
